# COPREPAN 3.0 -- ignore rules.
#
# Principles (AGENTS.md, "Working-tree hygiene"):
#   * Corpus data, raw captures, derived layers, runtime state and model caches never live in the
#     checkout; they live under the storage roots resolved from the environment. The rules below
#     are the second line of defence for a file that lands here anyway.
#   * Every rule is anchored or extension-specific and says why the file is not versioned.
#   * No blanket rule on a structured-text format: `*.json`, `*.jsonl`, `*.yml`, `*.csv` are NOT
#     ignored. Registries, configs, manifests, ledger snapshots and compact evidence are versioned.
#   * Small documented test fixtures stay trackable: see the negation block at the end.

# --- Python environments, caches, build products (regenerable) ---------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Secrets and workstation-specific configuration (never versioned) ---------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
/secrets/
# Storage roots are resolved from the environment; a file holding an absolute local or network
# path is workstation state, not architecture (docs/storage/INDEX.md).
/config/*.local.yml
/config/*.local.yaml
/config/*.local.json
/config/*.local.toml

# --- Editor, agent and OS state -----------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# Per-user agent settings; the shared project settings (.claude/settings.json) stay versioned.
.claude/settings.local.json
/.worktrees/

# --- Logs and temporary files (operational, regenerable, not evidence) --------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.part
/tmp/
/scratch/

# --- Runtime state and databases ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Ledgers, frontiers and job state belong to the runtime workspace outside the checkout. A SQLite
# file with its WAL/SHM siblings is live state; versioned evidence is a compact, hash-bound record
# exported from it, never the database.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.duckdb
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite-journal
/run_state/
/runtime/
/state/

# --- Corpus material: raw captures -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Fetched bytes are preservation objects (sealed WARC packs on the PRESERVATION root). They are
# large, they are third-party content, and git is not a preservation target.
*.warc
*.warc.gz
*.warc.zst
*.arc
*.arc.gz
*.cdx
*.cdxj
/raw/
/warc/
/packs/
/spool/

# --- Corpus material: derived layers, releases, exports ---------------------------------------------
# Extraction, normalisation, NLP and release layers are regenerable derived layers held in the
# layer store / on the storage roots. Columnar files are corpus output by construction.
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.feather
/data/
/corpus/
/layers/
/extracted/
/nlp_out/
/releases/
/exports/
/outputs/
/work/
/cache/
/workspace/

# --- Models and model caches (installed, never versioned) -----------------------------------------
/models/
/model_cache/
/.cache/
/hf_cache/
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth

# --- Archives ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default-ignored because an archive in the checkout is almost always a transport copy or a data
# dump. A deliberately versioned, hash-pinned evidence archive gets its own anchored negation rule
# with a comment naming the manifest that pins it.
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.tar.zst

# --- Fixtures stay trackable -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tests/fixtures/ holds SMALL, documented, non-production samples (recorded responses, miniature
# packs, miniature layer tables). tests/test_repository_contract.py bounds their size. These
# negations must stay the last block of this file.
!/tests/fixtures/**/*.warc
!/tests/fixtures/**/*.warc.gz
!/tests/fixtures/**/*.cdxj
!/tests/fixtures/**/*.parquet
!/tests/fixtures/**/*.sqlite
!/tests/fixtures/**/*.zip
!/tests/fixtures/**/*.log
